==========================================================================
NOAA data shipped in this package, and data fetched at run time
==========================================================================

- Noah land-surface tables in namgpu/data/fix/noah/ (VEGPARM.TBL, GENPARM.TBL, SOILPARM.TBL): NCEP's
  operational NMMB tables from the HMON package's NMMB fix set (hmon.v3.2.13/fix/nmmb), byte for byte
  (PROVENANCE.txt beside them). US Government data.
- NOAA fix files (CO2 history and monthly cycle, ozone climatology, solar constant, surface
  emissivity index) in namgpu/data/fix/, unmodified copies from the NOAA global fix bucket
  (fix/am/20220805; tools/fetch_fix.sh fetches them again). US Government data.
- Case inputs (NAM native analysis and boundary files, GFS 0.25 degree, MRMS), fetched from NOAA
  Open Data Dissemination by namgpu.init.init_fetch_case. US Government data.
- GMTED2010 terrain (USGS/NGA), read from the user's WPS geog set. Public domain.
- Start and boundary sources fetched at run time: NOAA RAP, HRRR, RRFS v1, GEFS v12 and AIGFS (US Government
  data, AWS NODD and NOMADS); ECMWF AIFS Single and IFS open data (CC BY 4.0, ECMWF).
- HRRR static soil classes (BNU soil, as NCEP's HRRR static file uses them), read from the user's geog set
  (bnu_soiltype_top, `gpuwm fetch-geog`) for the RUC option. Treated as US Government data, as the HRRR uses it.
- Monthly soil-moisture CDF tables (`woof-nam fetch-soil-cdf`, woof-nam release assets): built from the NOAA GFS
  and NAM soil analyses (US Government data) by tools/soil_start.
- Map basemap in namgpu/data/basemap/: Natural Earth 10m and 110m coastlines, lakes, land, ocean,
  borders and state lines (naturalearthdata.com, public domain) and the US Census Bureau
  cb_2023_us_county_5m county boundaries (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105), unmodified copies of
  the gpuwm 2.9.11 renderer bundle's assets/basemap.
- Climatological aerosol table namgpu/parm/nam_climaeropac_global.txt: NCEP format of the OPAC
  climatology, Hess, Koepke and Schult (1998), Bull. Amer. Meteor. Soc. 79, 831-844, as
  redistributed by NOAA in the GFS fix set.
